HTU-2062,loren,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 39.5""<br> <EOL>* Width: 12""<br> <EOL>* Height: 36.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Two Hump<br><br> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Large ruminant native to the desert regions of Asia & northern Africa. There are 2 kinds of camels: dromedary camel, which has 1 hump, & the Bactrian camel, w/c has 2 humps. Camel usually stands 2 m tall at the shoulders. The hump rises about 30 cm above the back. Feeds on grasses and shrubs. Gives birth to 1 foal after a gestation period of 390-410 days. Camels can go for long periods without water. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL>"
HTU-2441,loren,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 59""<br> <EOL>* Width: 24""<br> <EOL>* Height: 46.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing, Extra Large<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Lives in every land mass except Australia and Antarctica. Largest and most powerful of all land mammals. Eats about 225kg of grass, foliage and other vegetation a day and drinks about 136L of water at a time. Reaches a ht of 3m and the African elephant, 4 m. After a gestation period of 21 "" 22 months, usually one calf is born. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><i><b>Portraits in Nature</b></i> is a hand-crafted collection of realistic plush animals. Artists working in a socially responsible and environmentally responsible studio create each Hansa animal from portraits of the creature in its natural habitat.<br><br>"
HTU-2652,loren,51939,"<B>Details:</B><br> <EOL>* Length: 31""<br> <EOL>* Width: 9""<br> <EOL>* Height: 43.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Family Giraffidae. Tallest land mammal. Its long neck enables this unmistakable inhabitant of Africa's savannah to browse on vegetation which is its primary food. Male ave. 5.3 m in height & with its 40-cm tongue is able to reach high into acacia trees. About 15 months the cow bears a single calf, 1.7-2 m high, which can stand 20 minutes after birth. Lifespan: 25 yrs. in the wild. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Ride-On Hansa Animals</b><br> <EOL>This life-size piece has an exceptionally strong, yet lightweight, frame that provides ride-on experiences for children of all ages (up to 150 pounds).<br> <EOL> <EOL>Hansa structural metal frames generally allow the animals to be poseable, as their heads can be turned - and arms, wings and legs raised - to simulate movement. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>"
HTU-2676,loren,51946,"<b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Inhabits open plains & brush in Australia, Feeds chiefly upon roots, fruits, and herbage. Lays its eggs, which are dark green & about 10cm long, in a scooped out hole in the ground. Incubation takes almost 2 months. Attaining, height of 1.8 m The wings of the emu are mere rudiments hidden beneath the coarse, hair-like feathers of the body. The plumage is dull brown, darker on the head, neck, & mid-back. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL>"
HTU-2810,loren,51947,"<b>Details:</b> <br /> <EOL>* Length: 17.94""<br /> <EOL>* Width: 16.38""<br /> <EOL>* Height: 23.79""<br /> <EOL>* Position: Seated<br /><br /> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br /> <EOL>Found in areas of North America, Europe, and Asia. The fiercest and most aggressive bear. Females have their 1st young at 5 - 7 years old. Normally gives birth to 2 cubs. Able to reproduce up to almost 30yrs old. Eats enormous amounts of fish, berries & succulent plants, sometimes consuming 40 kg of food per day. Lifespan: Max. 30 yrs<br /><br /> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br /> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <br /><br /> <EOL> <EOL>"
HTU-3007,loren,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 53""<br> <EOL>* Width: 20""<br> <EOL>* Height: 25.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Ride-On<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Lives in every land mass except Australia and Antarctica. Largest and most powerful of all land mammals. Eats about 225kg of grass, foliage and other vegetation a day and drinks about 136L of water at a time. Reaches a ht of 3m and the African elephant, 4 m. After a gestation period of 21 "" 22 months, usually one calf is born.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3106,loren,51948,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 34.75""<br> <EOL>* Width: 17""<br> <EOL>* Height: 18.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Seated<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Found in Canada & Greenland. Coloured white, providing a camouflage when hunting, but under different light they may appear brownish, yellow or even light green. Eats berries, mussels, but mostly they eat ringed seals. After mating, female makes a den in the snow and will hibernate during the coldest months. Cubs, usually 2, are born 9 mos after mating. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3156,loren,51949,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 32""<br> <EOL>* Width: 14.5""<br> <EOL>* Height: 31""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Carrion-eating birds. Eurasian and African vultures probably descended eagle-like birds. Nearly all vultures are large birds with a naked head and hooked bill. Ranges from 63-70 cm. in length. American vultures are generally silent except for hissing and grunting sounds, such as those made by these turkey vulture nestlings.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3235,loren,51946,"<b>Details:</b><Br> <EOL>* Length: 17.75""<Br> <EOL>* Width: 15""<Br> <EOL>* Height: 43.5""<Br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<Br><Br> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><Br> <EOL>Found in Australia and Neighboring islands. They are Marsupials, a type of mammal that Gives birth to young 25 mm long approximately. Has pouch into which the young Joey crawls after it is born. The Joey remains in the pouch for some 190 days before it leaves for short periods. For such large animals they move easily, with leaps of 8-9 ms in length. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><Br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL>"
HTU-3261,loren,51949,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 29.5""<br> <EOL>* Width: 8.75""<br> <EOL>* Height: 32.75""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing, No Stand Included<br><br> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Common name for birds having exceptionally long legs and long, highly flexible necks. When feeding, flamingos dip the head under water & scoop backward with the head upside down. Males reach 155cm in height. Greater flamingo breeds in standing water or on low islands in shallow ponds, in which the 1 egg (rarely 2) is laid. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>Note: 4777 has been redesigned for 2014 to include a stand. Please specify whether you want a stand or not when placing your order. We will do our best to accommodate your request. Thank you. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3266,loren,51948,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 6.75""<br> <EOL>* Width: 9""<br> <EOL>* Height: 30""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Flightless aquatic birds of the southern hemisphere. Most have a white breast & black & head,has red, orange or yellow patches on the head and neck. Emperor penguin, may attain a ht. of more than 120 cm. King penguin, from 91-97cm in ht. Mostly lays 2 eggs, Incubation vary to species. Feed on fish, cuttlefish, crustaceans, and other small sea animals. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3268,loren,51949,<b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL>
HTU-3349,loren,51947,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 53""<br> <EOL>* Width: 13""<br> <EOL>* Height: 60"" (from the floor to the top of the antlers)<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Family Cervidae. Range through the Americas, Europe, Asia and North Africa. Range in size from the European elk or moose, which may reach a shoulder height of 2.35 m, and South American pudu, which can be as little as 25 cm high at the shoulder. Female gives birth once a year, usually to 1-2 fawns. Gestation period is from 160 days. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
