HTU-3568,loren,51939,"<b>Details:</b><Br> <EOL>* Length: 39""<Br> <EOL>* Width: 25""<Br> <EOL>* Height: 22""<Br> <EOL>* Position: Large, Lying, Majestic<Br><Br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><Br> <EOL>Family felidae. Lived Throughout Africa, Europe, Middle East, Asia, North America, South America. Measures up to 250 cm in length, not including the tail, Which measures 90-105cm. Lady lion is in estrus, recurring state in which female is receptive to sexual activity, she mates repeatedly, After Gestation of 110 days, she gives birth to 1-4 young, Lions are carnivores. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><Br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL>"
HTU-3595,loren,51940,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 41""<br> <EOL>* Width: 16""<br> <EOL>* Height: 35""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Order Artiodactyla. Found extensively in Australia, New Zealand, South America, and the western United States. The length of the head & body averages about 1.5 m with a short tail, and an adult may weigh 75-200 kg. Ewes usually produce 1 or 2 lambs, although 5 have been recorded; they are born woolly & open- eyed. Gestation period is about 21 weeks.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
