HTU-3677,loren,51947,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 50""<br> <EOL>* Width: 14""<br> <EOL>* Height: 47.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Ride-On, Life Size<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Family Cervidae. Known as elk, ruminant mammal native of Canada to Mexico and conspecific w/ the red deer of Europe, northwestern Africa and Asia. Dark brown fur on the head and neck. Full-grown stag stands up to 1.5m high at the shoulder. Grazes and browse on grasses, twigs and leaves. The doe bears a single fawn. Wapiti is known in North America as the moose. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3772,loren,51940,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* General Length: 51.25 inches<br> <EOL>* Height from floor to the horse's BACK : 39 inches<br> <EOL>* Height from the floor to the NOSE : 33 inches<br> <EOL>* Height from the floor to the top of the head, not including the ears : 50 inches<br> <EOL>* Length of the horse from the ""butt"" to the tip of the nose: 55 inches<br> <EOL>* Width of the horse at the widest part of the belly: 13 inches<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL>"
HTU-3802,loren,51949,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 46""<br> <EOL>* Width: 15.75""<br> <EOL>* Height: 24.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Large with 46"" Wing Span<br> <EOL><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Found world-wide. Has long, pointed wings, spanning up to 1.5m which are perfectly adapted to flapping, soaring and gliding flight. Generally they are powerful predators, catching its prey on the ground or snatching it from treetops. Few are carrion feeders. Prey includes reptiles, birds & small mammals. Lays few eggs; most species hatch & rear only 1-2 nestlings. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3808,khairy,51940,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 43.31""<br> <EOL>* Width: 9.84""<br> <EOL>* Height: 35.43""<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-3863,khairy,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 42.75""<br> <EOL>* Width: 12""<br> <EOL>* Height: 49""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Family Equidae. Few mountain zebras left in the wild live in the mountain grasslands of southwest Africa. The pattern of their stripes are unique as individual human fingerprints. Zebra""s forage for grass for 60-80 per cent of a 24-hour period. Zebra""s averages about 1.2 m high. The female gives birth to one foal after a year of gestation. Lifespan Up to 28 years <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
