HTU-4042,khairy,51941,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 35""<br> <EOL>* Width: 27""<br> <EOL>* Height: 78""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Found in areas of North America, Europe, and Asia. The fiercest and most aggressive bear. Females have their 1st young at 5 - 7 years old. Normally gives birth to 2 cubs. Able to reproduce up to almost 30yrs old. Eats enormous amounts of fish, berries & succulent plants, sometimes consuming 40 kg of food per day. Lifespan: Max. 30 yrs <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4043,khairy,51948,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 40""<br> <EOL>* Width: 12""<br> <EOL>* Height: 15""<br> <EOL>* Position: Sleeping<br><br> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Found in Canada & Greenland. Coloured white, providing a camouflage when hunting, but under different light they may appear brownish, yellow or even light green. Eats berries, mussels, but mostly they eat ringed seals. After mating, female makes a den in the snow and will hibernate during the coldest months. Cubs, usually 2, are born 9 mos after mating. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
