HTU-4268,khairy,51946,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 33.46""<br> <EOL>* Width: 15.75""<br> <EOL>* Height: 33.86""<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4283,khairy,51948,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 48""<br> <EOL>* Width: 25""<br> <EOL>* Height: 20""<br> <EOL>* Position: Crouching<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Found in northern India, in the states bordering the Himalays & Central Asian Republics. Feeds on sheeps, goats, deer & other small mammals. Each litter contains 1-5 cubs, after a gestation period of 98-103 days. Reaches up to 1-1.3 m in length head & body, a tail 80-100cm. Spot on the leopard""s fur are arranged in distinct rows. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4307,khairy,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 66.93""<br> <EOL>* Width: 19.69""<br> <EOL>* Height: 37.4""<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4315,khairy,51954,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 24""<br> <EOL>* Width: 22<br> <EOL>* Height: 24<br> <EOL>* Position: Seated as Chairman of the Board<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Adapted to life on the ground and avoid forests; They have strong, elongated jaws, large cheek pouches in w/c they store food, & eyes close together. They have overhanging brows & strong limbs. Able to distinguish colors & have keen sense of smell. Eats worms, insects, reptiles, crabs, mollusks, small mammals, fruits, & young shoots. Gestation period of about 6 months, and usually bears 1 offspring. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4325,khairy,51954,"<b>Details:</b><Br> <EOL>* Length: 51.97""<Br> <EOL>* Width: 25.98""<Br> <EOL>* Height: 66.93""<Br> <EOL><Br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><Br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL>"
HTU-4329,khairy,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 70""<br> <EOL>* Width: 15.5""<br> <EOL>* Height: 41""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing 6' L x 41"" tall<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Largest cat in the world. 3 major sub-species :Siberian,Bengal,Sumatra. Modern tiger have originated Northern Asia and spread southward thereafter, crossing the Himalayas. Measures 1.4""2.8m long not including the tail, which is 69 - 95 cm in length. Diet varies from deer, cattle, frogs and fish; carrion is also eaten. Bears 1-6 cubs, which stays w/ the mother for 2 yrs. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4351,khairy,51941,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 48""<br> <EOL>* Width: 32<br> <EOL>* Height: 48""<br> <EOL>* Position: Sitting<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Bear-like animal that has dense white fur with black markings on its ears, limbs, shoulders & around its eyes. Tail is stubby. Lives in pairs & small groups in bamboo forests-on which they feed""of the mountains in western China and in the Tibetan Himalaya. The cubs are born in late winter. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4446,khairy,51941,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 41.34""<br> <EOL>* Width: 15.75""<br> <EOL>* Height: 25.59""<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4489,khairy,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 32.28""<br> <EOL>* Width: 9.84""<br> <EOL>* Height: 35.43""<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>Portraits in Nature is a hand-crafted collection of realistic plush animals. Artists working in a socially responsible and environmentally responsible studio create each Hansa animal from portraits of the creature in its natural habitat. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>The Hansa Story</b><br> <EOL>Artisan hand sew the animals ""inside out"", an old world tradition that results in the mininization of seams, and their bodies are carefully ""sculpted"" to create ""musculature"" and ""features"" like movement in a walking or sitting position that are unique to each creature. On average, there are 42 separate pieces required to make each animal, that must be combined by a team of truly creative artists to create the distinctly realistic features that characterize HANSA animals. (Some animals have as many as 240 different parts!) Each animal is individually hand sewn, to give it a unique ""personality"", there are more than 860 different fabrics and man-made furs from which the ""coat"" and ""hides"" are made, along with over 6000 sets of different eyes, whiskers, claws, noses, and related accessories allocated for creating these wonderful plush animals. Stuffing emphasizes careful attention to the placement of the highest quality man-made materials. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>When you hold these wonderfully ""life-like"" animals, you will see and feel HANSA's emphasis on quality, which is a result of careful attention to design, custom fabric selection, cutting, sewing, stuffing, eye placement, feature creation, framing, air brushing and finishing. Since each animal is hand sewn, there will be slight variations in appearance."
HTU-4509,khairy,51947,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 33""<br> <EOL>* Width: 9""<br> <EOL>* Height: 38.5""<br> <EOL>* Note: ""lightweight but strong framing"" - best for smaller children<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Ride-On Deer</b><br> <EOL>Stunningly realistic, this remarkable White-Tail Deer is the perfect affordable gift for someone or centerpiece for your own collection or display! Equipped with our lightweight but strong framing, it's the perfect ride-on animal for smaller children! <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Family Cervidae. Range through the Americas, Europe, Asia and North Africa. Range in size from the European elk or moose, which may reach a shoulder height of 2.35 m, and South American pudu, which can be as little as 25 cm high at the shoulder. Female gives birth once a year, usually to 1-2 fawns. Gestation period is from 160 days. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4543,khairy,51941,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 29.5""<br> <EOL>* Width: 12""<br> <EOL>* Height: 24.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Walking on All 4's<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Bear-like animal that has dense white fur with black markings on its ears, limbs, shoulders & around its eyes. Tail is stubby. Lives in pairs & small groups in bamboo forests-on which they feed""of the mountains in western China and in the Tibetan Himalaya. The cubs are born in late winter. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
