HTU-4717,khairy,51949,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 19.75""<br> <EOL>* Width: 4""<br> <EOL>* Height: 28""<br> <EOL>* Position: Large, Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>All except the Congo peafowl of Africa are native to Asia. Males are about 9cm long. Females, which are buffy below, mottled with brown & black above, are about 63 cm long. Often called the ring necked pheasant because of the white ring on the neck of males of several of the 34 sub- species. As many as 15 or more species of pheasant are endangered. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL>"
