HTU-4731,khairy,51939,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 55.25""<br> <EOL>* Width: 17.75""<br> <EOL>* Height: 41.5""<br> <EOL>* Position: Walking, Life Size<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Lived Throughout Africa, Europe, Middle East, Asia, North America, South America. Measures up to 250 cm in length, not including the tail, Which measures 90-105cm. Lady lion is in estrus, recurring state in which female is receptive to sexual activity, she mates repeatedly, After Gestation of 110 days, she gives birth to 1-4 young, Lions are carnivores. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4812,khairy,51941,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 16.5""<br> <EOL>* Width: 18.87""<br> <EOL>* Height: 36.75<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Smallest of North America""s bears and is said to be the least aggressive. Feeds mainly on all kinds of vegetation and plant material, fish & carrion .Has a length of 1.3 - 1.l8 m. No. of young is 1-5 depending on the region and a gestation of 220 days. It is the inspiration for the original ""teddy bear"". <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
HTU-4883,khairy,51947,"<b>Details:</b><br> <EOL>* Length: 94.5""<br> <EOL>* Width: 31.5""<br> <EOL>* Height: 72""<br> <EOL>* Position: Standing, Life Size<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Animal Facts:</b><br> <EOL>Family of bovidae. One of the largest wild cattle in the world. Can reach up to 2m tall, 3m long & weigh 450-900kgs.Has a thick brown fur coat that keeps them warm in the harsh winter. It has a broad heads w/ horns, humped shoulders and thin limbs. It can run up to 38miles per hour. Mature at 3 years of age and have life expectancy of 18-22 years in the wild. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Age Group:</b><br> <EOL>The Recommended age for Hansa animals is 3 and up to comply with ASTM93 safety standards. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>"
